{title: I Love Thy Kingdom, Lord}
{artist: Timothy Dwight / Aaron Williams}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Evangelical Hymnal (Harrisburg, Pennsylvania: Evangelical Publishing House, 1921), # 17)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I love Thy king[D]dom, Lord,
[G]The house of [Am]Thine [G]ab[D]ode,
[D]The [G]church our [D]blessed Re[G]deem[Em]er [D]saved
[G]With [C]His [Am]own pre[D7]cious [G]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I love Thy church, [D]O God.
[G]Her walls be[Am]fore [G]Thee [D]stand,
[D]Dear [G]as the [D]apple [G]of [Em]Thine [D]eye,
[G]And [C]writ[Am]ten on [D7]Thy [G]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]If e’er to bless [D]Thy sons
[G]My voice or [Am]hands [G]de[D]ny,
[D]These [G]hands let [D]useful [G]skills [Em]for[D]sake,
[G]This [C]voice [Am]in si[D7]lence [G]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[G]Jesus, Thou friend [D]divine,
[G]Our Savior [Am]and [G]our [D]king,
[D]Thy [G]hand from [D]every snare [G]and [Em]foe
[D]Shall [G]great [C]de[Am]liver[D7]ance [G]bring.
{end_of_verse}
